A distinct part of a :term[process].

:::note
A step contributes directly to achieving the intended outcome of the process.
:::

:::note
Stages that occur before a process begins or only after the process outcome has been achieved are not steps. Initiating a process or acknowledging successful completion does not constitute a step. Only distinct units of interaction required to progress through the process are counted as steps.
:::


:::note
A review stage is a step when it requires reviewing information as part of the process before confirmation or progression (for example, reviewing order details before placing an order). Passive reading or viewing of information is not a review step.
:::

:::note
The following are not considered steps unless they require a meaningful action to achieve the intended outcome of the process:
* success pages or messages presented after completion;
* confirmation receipts;
* thank-you pages or messages;
* completion summaries presented after submission;
* opening a tooltip;
* expanding an accordion when the expanded content does not require action to continue the process;
* displaying contextual help. 
:::
